### Numbers

JavaScript has two built-in numeric types: Number and BigInt.

The Number type is an [IEEE 754 64-bit double-precision floating point value](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Double_precision_floating-point_format), which means integers can be safely represented between [-(2<sup>53</sup> − 1)](/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Number/MIN_SAFE_IN

